Name: swap
Signature: void swap(int* a, int* b)
Description: /**
 * @brief Swap the values of two integers.
 *
 * Exchanges the values pointed to by a and b. Both pointers must be valid
 * and non-NULL; the function modifies the integers in place.
 *
 * @param a Pointer to the first integer. Must not be NULL.
 * @param b Pointer to the second integer. Must not be NULL.
 *
 * @return None.
 */
Dependencies: None

FUNCTION IMPLEMENTATION:
```c
// C program for the function called swap
// Contains target function implementation and dependency signatures

// Target function implementation
void swap(int* a, int* b)
{
    int t = *a;
    *a = *b;
    *b = t;
}

```

